BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cmdev.petalumachamber.biz/events/details/medic-first-aid-cpr-and-aed-training-04-11-2026-12732"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Medic First Aid CPR and AED Training
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T083000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T123000
UID:251210sWh0D0p4l0WFGdfbWklV5g
DESCRIPTION:Course Description: This course goes a step beyond basic CPR. 
 In this four-hour class\, students will learn information and skills to pr
 ovide effective emergency care to an injured or ill person before first re
 sponders arrive. The workplace is the focus\, using industrial and office 
 settings for the scenario-based learning environment. CPR\, plus other lif
 esaving skills including bleeding control\, choke saving\, hazardous condi
 tions awareness\, and an introduction to the AED. Each students receives a
  manual\, instruction\, mannequin use and Medic First Aid card valid for t
 wo years. Course Audience: The class-of-choice for non-medical people\, th
 is class is the perfect course for any individual who would like to be pre
 pared to respond to a cardiac emergency\, anytime and anywhere. Great for 
 on-site training for employees who have a duty to respond to a cardiac eme
 rgency due to job responsibilities or regulatory requirements.
LOCATION:Petaluma Valley Hospital
URL:https://cmdev.petalumachamber.biz/events/details/medic-first-aid-cpr-a
 nd-aed-training-04-11-2026-12732
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"GoLocal Cooperative": "https://golocal.coop/event/march-against-stomach-cancer/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:golocal_coop
X-SOURCE:GoLocal Cooperative
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T110000
DTSTAMP:20260411T065655
CREATED:20260303T042228Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260303T042228Z
UID:10016786-1775896200-1775905200@golocal.coop
SUMMARY:March Against Stomach Cancer
DESCRIPTION:Our Annual March Against Stomach Cancer is to honor those we have lost and the more than one million people worldwide who are fighting this disease. In Memory of Sonoma Valley Resident\, John Cardinale\, is our primary west coast awareness and fundraising event to support stomach cancer research\, awareness\, and program initiatives of No Stomach For Cancer. \nAll proceeds from the $40 registration fee go to fund stomach cancer patient and caregiver programs and include an Official Event t-shirt. With your participation\, we can support stomach cancer research that needs funding now so that we can discover life-giving treatments and alternatives to stomach removal.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/march-against-stomach-cancer/
LOCATION:Spring Lake Regional Park\, 393 Violetti Rd\, Santa Rosa\, CA
CATEGORIES:Kids and Family,Other,Recreation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://golocal.coop/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/March-against-stomach-cancer-s.jpg
GEO:38.4542;-122.649
