SUMMARY:Guided Nature Walk at Anderson Mars
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T083000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T110000
UID:260408_ir-DIM8E0GJKI-Cat-cYQ
DESCRIPTION:Description Guided Nature Walk Saturday\, April 11\, 2026 at 8
 :30am at Anderson Marsh State Historic Park Join us for a guided nature wa
 lk on Saturday\, April 11 at 8:30am. Come and see what spring is bringing 
 to the park. The April nature walk will be led by Roberta Lyons\, a volunt
 eer State Parks docent and President of the Anderson Marsh Interpretive As
 sociation. The walk will begin at 8:30am and will last between 1-1/2 and t
 wo hours. The route taken on the walk will depend on the weather and the c
 ondition of the trails. There is no charge for the guided nature walk and 
 parking is free for those attending. No pets are permitted on the park tra
 ils which pass through a protected Natural Preserve. Bring binoculars and 
 meet in the parking lot at 8:15am for time to experience the early morning
  wildlife that can be found in the Ranch House picnic area. Everyone is in
 vited to take a walk in the park\, learn about what this Lake County jewel
  has to offer\, and experience the benefits of getting out into nature for
  some healthy exercise. Anderson Marsh State Historic Park is located on H
 wy 53\, between Lower Lake and Clearlake.
URL:https://support.lakecochamber.com/events/details/guided-nature-walk-at
 -anderson-mars-20391
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
