 ster Gardeners of Napa County.** ﻿\n\n**25 varieties to choose from** 
 — newcomers & old favorites — you are sure to find the perfect tomato 
 plants to add to your garden and your table. Heirloom and specially select
 ed hybrids\, such as: **Early Girl**\, **Brandywine\, Black Krim\, Japan
 ese Black Trifele\, Pink Berkeley Tie Dye\, Cherokee Green\, Captain Lucky
 \, Black Cherry\, Sungold\, Sunrise Bumblebee\, Napa Chardonnay\, Sweet Ca
 rneros Pink\, Amish Paste\, San Marzano II and more!**﻿\n\nFind more inf
 ormation on this sale\, a list with descriptions of all of the varietals\,
  and growing tips: https://ucanr.edu/site/uc-master-gardeners-napa-county
 /tomato-plant-sale-and-education-day-event\n\n Saturday\, April 11\, 9am-
 until sold out! 1710 Soscol Ave\, Napa (just south of Central Valley Hardw
 are).  $5 each. **Cash & checks only.** \n\n﻿All proceeds benefit our 
 Master Gardeners' educational programs for Napa County residents.
