DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T161500
UID:250801aJy6mnoexkO6IrdoQ5fPOw
DESCRIPTION:**A Kingdom at Risk\, a Beat That Won’t Quit\, and Love That
  Rules All!**\n\n***“It’s a feel good riot from start to finish.“* 
 — Jay Darcy\, Mancunion Media Group** \n\n**Get ready for a wild\, laugh
 -out-loud adventure with *HEAD OVER HEELS*—the electrifying musical come
 dy from the creative forces behind Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, Avenue Q\, 
 and Spring Awakening! Nominated for *Outstanding New Broadway Musical* in 
 2019 and powered by the chart-topping hits of the legendary all-female roc
 k band The Go-Go’s\, this high-energy show features beloved anthems like
  “We Got the Beat\,” “Our Lips Are Sealed\,” “Vacation\,” “H
 eaven is a Place on Earth\,” and “Mad About You.”**\n\n**Join a spir
 ited royal family on a whirlwind quest to save their kingdom from doom—o
 nly to realize that the key to their future isn’t written in fate\, but 
 in their own hearts. Packed with irresistible music\, over-the-top comedy\
 , and a whole lot of love\, *HEAD OVER HEELS* is a dazzling\, feel-good sp
 ectacle that will have you dancing in your seat!**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays 
 & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: Two hours
 \, 15 mins including intermission\n\nThursdays Adult $33Fri/Sat Eve Adult 
 $44.95\; Senior $38.95\; Under 18 $31.95Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $55.95\; Sen
 ior $48.95Value seating $37.95\\*All prices include fees(707) 523-4185**bo
 xoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/head-over-heels/
X-SOURCE:GoLocal Cooperative, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.farmtrails.org/event/grafting-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Grafting Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T160000
UID:260408V3RqF58B10aY_TN2KU5gzw
DESCRIPTION:Join Sonoma Ecology Center and Sonoma County Ag \\+ Open Space
  for a 2 hour grafting workshop at Sonoma Garden Park with local horticult
 urist Thomas Perot! Your workshop registration fee includes your very own 
 fruit tree—and the knowledge and skills to care for it!  \n\nThis worksh
 op will cover: \n\n— Grafting techniques for different species of fruit 
 trees.\n\n— Rootstock incompatibilities.\n\n— How to choose the best f
 ruiting varieties for the rootstock you have.\n\n— Best seasons to graft
  different fruit trees.\n\n— Proper sanitization practices and how to ke
 ep grafting knives sharp. \n\nThings to keep in mind: \n\n— Wear proper 
 footwear for wet/muddy and uneven paths.\n\n— Dress in layers.\n\n— Br
 ing: grafting knife and shears \\(if you have them\\)\, sun protection\, a
 nd a water bottle.\n\n— The small parking lot can fill up quickly\, so a
 rrive early to allow yourself enough time to park on the road if needed. \
 n\nThis outing is FREE to attend thanks to the voters of Sonoma County who
  fund the work of Ag \\+ Open Space with a quarter cent sales tax. \n\nAbo
 ut Sonoma Garden Park: Sonoma Garden Park was protected by Ag \\+ Open Spa
 ce in November of 2011 for recreation and preservation of its natural reso
 urces\, and learning classroom environment for agriculture field trips for
  nearby elementary schools through Sonoma Ecology Center’s “Growing Di
 scovery” program. The 6-acre property\, hidden in eastern Sonoma\, is an
  incredible public park and working garden site in Sonoma Valley\, home of
  a wide array of habitats alongside sustainably designed systems for both 
 agriculture use and landscaping purposes. \n\nSign up here:
LOCATION:Sonoma Garden Park
URL:https://www.farmtrails.org/event/grafting-workshop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
