SUMMARY:Our Phones Left Home: Local Children's Book Author Read-Aloud
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T120000
UID:260407ig41FKWSu0yDrD-aF4z-0Q
DESCRIPTION:**Sunday\, April 12th**\n\nJoin us for a read aloud of "Our Ph
 ones Left Home" by local author John Edwards! This story highlights the im
 portance of time away from our screens and healthy digital boundaries. We'
 ll have kids activities\, live music by Dave Fromer\, and snacks!\n\nWith 
 humor\, warmth\, and irresistible illustrations\, Our Phones Left Home! 
 playfully explores digital balance in a way that invites families to redis
 cover the joys of unplugged living. Join Tex\, Phonicia\, and their parent
 s on a laugh-out-loud journey that reminds us that sometimes the best conn
 ections don't need Wi-Fi.\n\n**Time:** 11am - 12pm\n\n**Location:** Usher 
 Gallery\, Petaluma
LOCATION:Usher Gallery
URL:https://ushergallerypetaluma.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
