SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Symphony - Celebrate America!
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T150000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T160000
UID:2512174WlLx2ouTUCdAlr_cpmSfQ
DESCRIPTION:Snoopy Family Concert Series\n\nCelebrate America!\n\nApril 12
 \, 2026 at 3:00 pm\n\nWeill Hall\, Green Music Center\n\nFrancesco Lecce-C
 hong\, conductor\n\nJaco Wong\, guest conductor\n\nJesse Barrett\, vocalis
 t\n\nAmelia Chun\, piano\n\nAARON COPLAND: Hoe-Down from Rodeo\n\nJOHN STA
 FFORD SMITH & FRANCIS SCOTT KEY: The Star-Spangled Banner\n\nWILLIAM GRANT
  STILL: Symphony No. 1\, Afro-American Symphony\n\nSorrow – Adagio \\[ex
 cerpt TBD\\]\n\nSCOTT JOPLIN: The Entertainer\n\nAARON COPLAND: Old Americ
 an Songs\n\nSimple Gifts\n\nI Bought Me a Cat\n\nGEORGE GERSHWIN Ferde Gro
 fé\, arranger: Rhapsody in Blue\n\n\\[excerpts TBD\\]\n\nGABRIELA LENA FR
 ANK: The Mestizo Waltz from Three Latin American Dances\n\nPAUL DOOLEY: So
 noma Strong for Orchestra\n\n\\[excerpt TBD\\]\n\nLEONARD BERNSTEIN Mauric
 e Peress\, arranger: Overture to West Side Story\n\nSAMUAL A. WARD & KATHA
 RINE LEE BATES: America the Beautiful\n\nCelebrate America in Music and Sp
 irit!\n\nGather the whole family for a fun\, inspiring concert honoring th
 e 250th anniversary of the United States\, featuring music that reflects t
 he rich and varied voices of the American landscape.\n\nTap your toes to C
 opland’s Hoe-Down and sway to the timeless beauty of Simple Gifts\, sing
  along to America the Beautiful and The Star-Spangled Banner\, and feel th
 e rhythm of Scott Joplin’s The Entertainer. Experience a show-stopping p
 erformance from pianist Amelia Chun of the Santa Rosa Symphony Youth Orche
 stra\, featured in excerpts from Gershwin’s Rhapsody in Blue.\n\nExplore
  the soundscape of America at this joyful celebration of country.\n\nProgr
 ams\, dates\, artists\, and prices are subject to change without notice. T
 ickets are subject to availability.\n\n© Peanuts Worldwide LLC
LOCATION:Green Music Center
