SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T160000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T170000
UID:260212EThVMU8D-EuXEw1mHOFRNg
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on **Sunda
 ys from 4:00 – 5:00 PM** **at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulu
 pa Ave.\, Room #4\, Santa Rosa**. Contact: Abigail (707) 293-5888. You may
  view all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northb
 ayoa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emoti
 onal\, and physical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and livi
 ng by their spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a d
 iet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of e
 ating.\n\nOA does **not** endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is ca
 using problems in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery
  is possible\, and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa
 .org/\n\n**Find a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/in-conversation-with-inez-storer?aff=cityspark"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:In Conversation with Inez Storer
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T160000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T170000
UID:260408Qtsi5GRbv0Ga7iYy9JguJA
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, April 12\, 4:00-5:00pm$15 members\; $20 non-members\n
 \nAn afternoon conversation about Inez's approach to artmaking\, her famil
 y history and the stories that inform her art. There will be time for ques
 tions. \n\nStorer lives in Inverness\, California\, and has a studio in Po
 int Reyes Station. Born in Santa Monica in 1933 to a Catholic father and J
 ewish mother\, she spent time on Hollywood movie sets where her father wor
 ked as an art director. Influenced by stage design\, her work often create
 s a sense of &ldquo\;theatrical space&rdquo\; and reflects her ancestry. S
 hortly before her death\, her mother revealed that she had fled Germany to
  escape Nazism. Storer later learned of cousins who escaped on the Kindert
 ransport. The frustration of being kept from the truth has infused her wor
 k with a distinct angst. Her work is held in many collections including th
 e Jewish Museum in New York\, Manetti Shrem Museum of Art at UC Davis\, Oa
 kland Museum of Art \, the de Young Museum\, San Jos&eacute\; Museum of Ar
 t\, Monterey Museum of Art\, Missoula Museum of Art\, and the National Mus
 eum of American Jewish History.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/in-conversation-with-inez-
 storer?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
