SUMMARY: Drawing Fundamentals
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Elysia Rose Cordero\nDate: Sunday\, April 12th\nT
 ime: 1:00PM-3:00PM\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\nFee: $45\n\n\nThis class 
 provides a foundational introduction to the art of drawing\, designed for
  absolute beginners or those with experience. The session focuses on brid
 ging the gap between seeing and recreating form on paper. Key areas of fo
 cus include:\n\n  * Supply Essentials: A comprehensive look at the specif
 ic materials required for drawing\, including the differences between pen
 cil grades (H vs. B) and eraser types.\n  * Proper Technique: Guidance on
  how to properly hold and use drawing supplies to achieve varying line we
 ights and textures while maintaining control.\n  * The Artist’s Eye: Exer
 cises dedicated to improving hand-eye coordination and observational skil
 ls\, teaching students to draw what they actually see rather than what th
 ey think they see.\n\n\nTeacher contact: Elysia.rose.cordero@gmail.com ma
 ilto:Elysia.rose.cordero@gmail.com\n\nCourse fee: $45 You are welcome to 
 bring your own supplies or send the teacher an email to have supplies pro
 vided at an additional fee.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Drawing
