BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Santa Rosa Junior College": "https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/17769-the-sleep-lab-building-better-habits-for-sleep"}
X-SOURCE-ID:srjc
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260416T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260416T180000
LOCATION:Lindley STEM Center\, Room 138 - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:The Sleep Lab: Building Better Habits for Sleep
DESCRIPTION:Student Health PEERs are excited to host an engaging and inte
 ractive workshop focused on building better sleep habits to support stude
 nts' overall well-being and daily performance.  Workshop Details:Guest Sp
 eaker: Megan Blocker is a therapist trainee at SRJC Student Psychological
  Services and a doctoral candidate at the PAU-Stanford PsyD Consortium. S
 he is currently involved in the Computational Psychiatry\, Neuroimaging\,
  and Sleep Lab (CoPsyN) at Stanford University School of Medicine\, where
  she is developing skills in assessing and treating sleep disorders.Peer-
 led activities: Peers will lead hands-on activities including creating yo
 ur own aromatherapy remedies and sleep journals as practical strategies f
 or improving sleep quality.  Whether you're looking to feel more rested\,
  improve focus\, or simply learn more about healthy sleep practices\, thi
 s workshop offers valuable tools in a supportive and interactive environm
 ent.Visit the SHS website here! (https://shs.santarosa.edu/peers)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Student Health PEERs are excited to hos
 t an engaging and interactive workshop focused on building better sleep h
 abits to support students' overall well-being and daily performance.</p><
 p>  Workshop Details:<br /><br /><strong>Guest Speaker:</strong> Megan Bl
 ocker is a therapist trainee at SRJC Student Psychological Services and a
  doctoral candidate at the PAU-Stanford PsyD Consortium. She is currently
  involved in the Computational Psychiatry\, Neuroimaging\, and Sleep Lab 
 (CoPsyN) at Stanford University School of Medicine\, where she is develop
 ing skills in assessing and treating sleep disorders.</p><p><strong>Peer-
 led activities:</strong> Peers will lead hands-on activities including cr
 eating your own aromatherapy remedies and sleep journals as practical str
 ategies for improving sleep quality.<br /><br />  Whether you're looking 
 to feel more rested\, improve focus\, or simply learn more about healthy 
 sleep practices\, this workshop offers valuable tools in a supportive and
  interactive environment.</p><p><a href="https://shs.santarosa.edu/peers"
  target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit the SHS website here!</a></p>
UID:20260416T230000Z-17769@calendar.santarosa.edu
