X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/our-wild-watershed-tree-swallow-monitoring-with-linda-len-sheryl/18409974/2026-04-16T17", "Press Democrat": "https://OWWTreeswallows26.eventbrite.com"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/our-wild-watershed-tree-swallow-monitoring-with-linda-len-sheryl/18409974/2026-04-16T17"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Our Wild Watershed- Tree Swallow Monitoring with Linda\, Len & She
 ryl
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T173000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T183000
UID:260326JOnUr2iO6kSWoKs4GS7kSg
DESCRIPTION:The Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation invites you to a presentat
 ion on Tree Swallow Monitoring with experienced nest box volunteers. Learn
  about these fascinating birds and how local efforts help support their po
 pulations.\n\nHave you ever noticed the beautiful tree swallows around you
 ? With their shimmering\, colorful wings and graceful\, jet-like flight\, 
 they are a joy to watch as they swoop and zoom through the air in search o
 f insects. Their soft\, musical bird songs and agile movements make them o
 ne of the most captivating sights in wetland and open habitats. You may ha
 ve even spotted them near local Laguna areas or seen them nesting in bird 
 boxes\, raising their young just a few feet from where people pass by.\n\n
  The Petaluma Wetlands Alliance \\(PWA\\) has supported local bird popula
 tions through its nest box program for nearly 20 years. Volunteers install
 \, maintain\, and monitor 60 nest boxes across six locations\, providing s
 afe nesting sites for species like tree swallows and bluebirds while track
 ing their nesting success. PWA also participates in the Cornell Lab of Orn
 ithology NestWatch citizen science program\, contributing data that helps 
 scientists better understand bird populations and environmental changes.\n
 \nPresenters:\n\nLinda Sheppard\, coordinator of the NestWatch program\, a
 long with Len Nelson and Sheryl Nadeau\, are long-time nest box builders a
 nd highly experienced monitors. They bring years of knowledge and dedicati
 on to bird conservation and community science.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/our-wild-watershed-tree
 -swallow-monitoring-with-linda-len-sheryl/18409974/2026-04-16T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/drawing-in-joy/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Drawing in Joy: Laughing with Life\, a Dance on Paper
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T173000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T200000
UID:260324VQaudcg2BEK6rkqJRtAg9g
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nThursdays\, April 9 – 30\, 2026 5:30 PM – 8:00
  PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Cat
 egories: Drawing & Painting\, Extended Classes\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and old
 er\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$175\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nSee Required List\n\
 nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$175\n\nExpress joy through drawing. Build sk
 ills in sketching\, composition & landscapes. Boost focus\, creativity\, c
 onnection & well-being.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nWhen we feel a sense of joy\
 , it is natural to express that feeling from our body. We may use our voic
 e and sing\, we may dance\, and we may use our hands in creative expressio
 n. By drawing we leave a mark of that expression. This course is shaped wi
 th skill building exercises to improve eye-hand coordination with quick sk
 etching and gesture drawing and practices of learning to see how to abstra
 ct shapes of light and dark for developing strong compositions. We will fo
 cus on landscape imagery from photos and drawing from setups in the studio
 . Drawing outside of class will be encouraged but not required. There are 
 many health benefits from drawing such as: improvements in cognitive focus
 \, freedom of expression with your hands\, the satisfaction that comes fro
 m seeing the world in a different way\, the social camaraderie of acceptan
 ce in the studio\, and the joy of doing something with your hands.\n\nRequ
 ired Materials List\n\nA good size sketch book for multimedia\n\nNewsprint
  drawing pad \\(12” x 18” or 18” x 24”\\)\n\nBlack pencils\, 6B so
 ft\n\nCompressed charcoal sticks\, black and white\n\nEraser\, kneaded rub
 ber\n\nEraser\, white vinyl\n\nBlack felt pens
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/drawing-in-joy/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
