UID:260407nn5xCewmv06LagUYxuTjAg
DESCRIPTION:Join **Yountville Library** for an evening with **Amelia Glase
 r\, UCSD Literature professor** and translator. She will share the story o
 f contemporary Ukrainian poets pushing language to its creative limit and 
 illustrating why poetry is still relevant in an increasingly complex world
 . \n\nTaste **Lost Valley Wines** with **Ivan Burdinskyi**\, a Ukrainian 
 winemaker who fled occupied Crimea\, and enjoy Ukrainian food by **Natalia
 's Dacha** as **Napa Valley To Ukraine**\, co-hosts of the event\,  celeb
 rates  Dr. Glaser's work and her hometown visit during National Poetry Mo
 nth.\n\nAmelia Glaser grew up in Yountville and graduated from Vintage Hig
 h School.\n\n**Napa Bookmine** will be on-site selling the books of Ukrain
 ian poets that she translated.
LOCATION:Yountville Community Center
URL:https://events.napalibrary.org/event/16005083
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
