BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:What About Age? Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T090000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T180000
UID:260318tOFpACNV2U2QFKvQvCfHUQ
DESCRIPTION:*What About Age?* art exhibit has arrived in Marin County! Or
 iginally displayed at NYU’s Kimmel Windows\, this exhibit explores ageis
 m through contemporary art\, featuring works by both local youth and senio
 r artists.\n\n*What About Age?* is an art exhibit and educational initiat
 ive designed to challenge stereotypes about aging\, address ageism and soc
 ial isolation\, and promote intergenerational dialogue through the lens of
  art.\n\nIn partnership with Youth in Arts\, the exhibit features artworks
  by local youth and senior artists\, showcasing how age intersects with cr
 eativity\, identity\, and experience. Under the guidance of Youth in Arts\
 , these emerging and established artists work side by side to create colla
 borative pieces\, fostering meaningful connections between generations and
  reflecting the exhibit’s core message: art is ageless.\n\nThe exhibit a
 lso includes artwork panels by New York-based writer and illustrator Aubre
 y Hirsch\, first displayed at NYU’s Kimmel Windows and originally organi
 zed by Stacey Gordon\, NYU’s Program Director of Next Phase Adult Caregi
 ving and Retirement at Work Life.\n\nThe new exhibition will be on view at
  the Marin County Civic Center galleries from January 26 to May 6\, 2026. 
 Works will be displayed on the first and third floor exhibits\, Monday to 
 Friday from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m.\n\nThe *What About Age?* art exhibit is prese
 nted by Marin Cultural Association in partnership with Marin Community Fou
 ndation and Youth in Arts. Beyond the art exhibit\, the *What About Age?* 
 initiative offers programming\, led by Vivalon\, designed to challenge age
 ism and provide resources for Marin County's growing aging population.
LOCATION:Marin County Civic Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://gratoncommunityclub.org", "Press Democrat": "https://gratoncommunityclub.org"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://gratoncommunityclub.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"April in Paris" - Flower Show and Plant Sale at the Graton Commun
 ity Club
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T090000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T160000
UID:260316F5x_kuGrLEGq2DSXwF0mzA
DESCRIPTION:This world in “transition” can be horrifying and at best i
 ntense\, so this Spring 2026 the Graton Community Club has chosen to look 
 back to another time and place\, “April in Paris”. We all need a littl
 e respite.\n\nWe are offering not only our signature theme-focused flower 
 arrangements and affordable spring garden plants and veggie starts\, but a
 n outing at "Café de Graton" in the dining room with a French-themed lunc
 heon\, beverages and homemade desserts\, all for $15.\n\nTake a welcome br
 eak from the intensity and join us on April 17 and 18 in downtown Graton. 
 Hours are 9am-4pm both days. You'll find one-of-a kind handmade crafts and
  novelties\, live local music and community connections. Then take that LO
 VE back into the world — we all need it. ALL are welcome\, Free admissio
 n. Proceeds from this event will go towards providing scholarships for loc
 al area students\, as well as helping maintain our historic building.
LOCATION:Graton Community Club
URL:https://gratoncommunityclub.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.farmtrails.org/event/sonoma-garden-park-volunteer-workday-dia-de-trabajo-voluntario-cada-tercer-viernes-del-mes/2026-04-17/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sonoma Garden Park Volunteer Workday | Día de trabajo voluntario 
 cada tercer viernes del mes
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T090000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T120000
UID:2604088MVxRDO2wkiCtry-dlLYDg
DESCRIPTION:\\[Español abajo\\] \n\nEvery 3rd Friday of the month from 9:
 00 am to 12:00 pm we welcome existing and new volunteers for a fun morning
  of work and community building at Sonoma Garden Park. Depending on the se
 ason activities include prepping fields\, planting\, harvesting\, weeding\
 , pruning trees and prepping produce for the seasonal Saturday Harvest mar
 ket.  \n\nJoin us for a fun opportunity to enjoy the bounty of each season
 \, and to share and learn from other gardeners. Existing and new volunteer
 s are encouraged to attend—no experience is necessary! Please be sure to
  bring your gardening gloves\, hat\, SPF and water. At noon you enjoy a li
 ght garden fresh lunch at our shady picnic area provided by Sonoma Ecology
  Center as a thank you to our wonderful volunteers! \n\nLos voluntarios ju
 egan un papel vital en el Garden Park. ¡Te invitamos a ensuciarte las man
 os cada tercer viernes de mes! Únete a nosotros de 9:00 am. a 12:00 pm y 
 conoce a los voluntarios existentes y nuevos. Las actividades incluyen des
 hierbe\, siembra\, poda y cosecha. Después del trabajo\, disfruta de un a
 lmuerzo ligero proporcionado por el Centro Ecológico de Sonoma. \n\nSonom
 a Garden Park está ubicado en 19996 7th St E\, Sonoma\, CA 95476 y es un 
 proyecto del Sonoma Ecology Center.
LOCATION:Sonoma Garden Park
URL:https://www.farmtrails.org/event/sonoma-garden-park-volunteer-workday-
 dia-de-trabajo-voluntario-cada-tercer-viernes-del-mes/2026-04-17/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
