DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T210000
UID:260324N6b8_KMsekaGOT-68MhkgA
DESCRIPTION:Cinnabar Theater presents The Christians by Lucas Hnath\n\nA p
 owerful\, thought-provoking drama about faith\, conviction\, and the cost 
 of standing by your beliefs.\n\nWhen a beloved megachurch pastor delivers 
 a sermon that challenges a core doctrine\, his congregation is thrown into
  turmoil. What follows is an intimate and gripping exploration of belief\,
  doubt\, leadership\, and community—inviting audiences to wrestle with b
 ig questions that linger long after the final moment on stage.\n\n• Warr
 en Theater\, Sonoma State University \\(Ives Hall\\)\, 1801 East Cotati Av
 e\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\n• April 10–26\, 2026\n\n• Fridays & S
 aturdays at 7:30 PM | Sundays at 2:00 PM\n\n• Special Talkback Post Show
 : Sunday\, April 19\n\nDirected by Nathan Cummings and featuring a stellar
  cast\, this minimalist\, emotionally resonant production is recommended f
 or mature audiences.\n\nTickets: cinnabartheater.org
LOCATION:Sonoma State University
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thechristians/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
