BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/dumpling-workshop-with-lani-chan-at-gold-ridge-organic-farms/18329506/2026-04-18T10", "Press Democrat": "https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/599710/dumpling-workshop-with-lani-chan"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/dumpling-workshop-with-lani-chan-at-gold-ridge-organic-farms/18329506/2026-04-18T10"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Dumpling Workshop with Lani Chan at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T130000
UID:260408dTgP8ed230mC0BcOzFegBA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a 3-hour hands-on dumpling workshop led by Lani Ch
 an\, founder of Hei Ma\, where you'll learn to make dumplings entirely fro
 m scratch — wrappers\, fillings\, and all. You'll start by making the do
 ugh using heirloom grain flours grown by our Sebastopol neighbor Farmer Ma
 i\, who will be on hand to share the story behind their remarkable grains.
  From there\, you'll form and cook vegetarian dumplings\, learn to make sc
 allion pancakes\, and pair everything with Hei Ma chili crisp and a specia
 l dipping sauce made with Gold Ridge Organic Farms Apple Cider Balsamic Vi
 negar.\n\nThe experience begins with a ride aboard our apple-themed trolle
 y out to the Apple Cottage\, where the class will take place surrounded by
  the beauty of the farm. Each guest will receive an apple-blossom pink apr
 on to take home and enjoy a refreshing citrus shrub alongside their freshl
 y made dumplings. Whether you're a seasoned home cook or a first-time dump
 ling maker\, this is an experience you won't forget — good food\, great 
 company\, and a deeper connection to the ingredients grown right here in S
 onoma County.\n\nLani Chan is the co-founder of Hei Ma \\(formerly known a
 s Big Spoon Sauce Co.\\)\, a Sonoma County-based small-batch sauce brand r
 ooted in Chinese culinary tradition and peak-season California produce. Wh
 at began as a chili crisp project in a Brooklyn apartment in 2019 has grow
 n into a community-driven food brand celebrated for its bold flavors and c
 ultural heart.\n\nMai Nguyen is an award-winning heirloom grain farmer\, m
 iller\, seed keeper\, and community organizer based right here in Sebastop
 ol. In 2024\, their work was recognized with the prestigious James Beard L
 eadership Award for their contributions to sustainability\, equity\, and j
 ustice in food systems\, collaborating with communities and coalitions to 
 shape food policy that uplifts marginalized farmers and promotes land sove
 reignty.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/dumpling-workshop-with-
 lani-chan-at-gold-ridge-organic-farms/18329506/2026-04-18T10
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.ButterAndEggDays.com", "Press Democrat": "http://www.ButterAndEggDays.com"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.ButterAndEggDays.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Butter & Egg Days Parade & Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T170000
UID:260408NbIfyLar6kmWgMZu3FncJA
DESCRIPTION:Theme: "America's Birthday - Petaluma Style"\n\n*Celebrating 
 250 years of independence\, ingenuity\, and small-town pride.*\n\n“Ameri
 cas’ Birthday – Petaluma Style” celebrates the nation’s 250th Birt
 hday by honoring Petaluma’s deep agricultural roots and hometown spirit.
  This year’s Butter & Egg Days Parade recognizes the farmers\, families\
 , immigrants\, makers\, entrepreneurs\, and creatives whose hard work\, im
 agination\, and ingenuity reflect the enduring American Dream. This celebr
 ation also pays respect to the Indigenous peoples who first stewarded this
  land\, the courage of our founders\, and the dedication of the dairy and 
 egg farming community that shaped our town. Rooted in community\, innovati
 on\, and independence\, the parade celebrates the small-town spirit that c
 ontinues to make Petaluma a vibrant place to call home. Head to Downtown P
 etaluma and celebrate with our community on this day of fun\, history\, an
 d local pride!\n\nParade participants incorporate the theme *“America's
  Birthday - Petaluma Style”* into their entry design. The theme gives n
 onprofits\, businesses\, organizations\, and individuals lots of options f
 or showing off their creativity in their designs. All parade entries will 
 be judged on how well their entry portrays this year's theme - winners ann
 ounced on the website! Check back later to see which entries take home the
  prizes and earn bragging rights.\n\nThe Butter & Egg Days festivities kic
 k off on Saturday\, **April 11** with the **Opening Ceremonies** at the
  Petaluma Historical Library and Museum (20 Fourth St)\, from Noon to 1pm.
  Mayor Kevin McDonnell will read a proclamation honoring the Grand Marshal
  and Good Egg. Come enjoy this display that shows the heart of our communi
 ty.\n\nOne week later on Saturday\, **April 18\,** the Butter & Egg Days
  **Parade** steps off at noon and marches through the historic downtown. 
 The parade showcases over 100 units with approximately 3\,000 participants
  and 200 volunteers. Clover Sonoma returns to lead the Clover **Kids’ P
 arade**\, which precedes the main parade at 11:30am with a procession of p
 reschoolers and primary grade youngsters and their families.\n\nThe parade
  is surrounded by a **Festival** that spreads over four city blocks from 
 10am-5pm offering a wide variety of food\, crafts\, beverage gardens\, two
  large kid areas\, live music\, and more! This annual event aims to bring 
 together the community for a day of fun and entertainment.\n\nThe followin
 g weekend\, Downtown Petaluma continues the celebration with the Annual Sp
 ring Antique Faire\, on Sunday\, **April 26**.\n\nHappy Butter & Egg Days
 !!!\n\nVisit ButterAndEggDays.com for more information!
LOCATION:Historic Downtown Petaluma
URL:http://www.ButterAndEggDays.com 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
