X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sonoma.com": "https://www.sonoma.com/event/spring-celebration-at-charlies-acres/", "North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sonoma.com/event/spring-celebration-at-charlies-acres/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sonoma.com": "https://www.sonoma.com/event/spring-celebration-at-charlies-acres/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sonoma_com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Sonoma.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T110000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T143000
DTSTAMP:20260411T135655
CREATED:20260316T220345
LAST-MODIFIED:20260316T220345
UID:59519-1776510000-1776522600@https://www.sonoma.com
SUMMARY:Spring Celebration at Charlie's Acres
DESCRIPTION:Charlie’s Acres hosts a family-friendly Spring Celebration\, inviting guests to enjoy a fun and meaningful day surrounded by rescued animals. Visitors can explore the sanctuary on a guided loop\, meet the animal residents\, and learn their rescue stories while offering gentle treats and affection.    The event also features festive food available for purchase\, a kid-friendly scavenger hunt\, and indoor and outdoor games for all ages\, with chances to win prizes. Designed to be both entertaining and educational\, the celebration offers a heartwarming way to connect with animals and the community.    Held rain or shine\, proceeds from the event support the lifelong care of over 150 rescued animals and fund free humane education programs for schools.
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/spring-celebration-at-charlies-acres/
LOCATION:3201 Napa Road, Sonoma, CA, 95476, United States
CATEGORIES:Celebration,Family Friendly,Outdoors
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://winecountry-media.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2026/03/16220333/649323053_922842930297726_3824496775125827991_n.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/2026-healdsburg-arts-festival/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:2025 Healdsburg Arts Festival- Call for Artists
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T170000
UID:2604070jjjnqM8BU25yhBjFBA5bw
DESCRIPTION:Now in our 13th year\, the Festival will include a day of loca
 l art for sale with over 30 participating artists\, music\, art workshops 
 for children\, a raffle\, food\, and good wine. Due to changes made by th
 e City of Healdsburg\, we will be holding the Festival from the Center and
  Plaza Street to the intersection of Center and North Street.  HCA is ded
 icated to celebrating art in the community with our annual cornerstone eve
 nt in downtown Healdsburg.\n\nPlease\, mark your calendars and plan to joi
 n in the fun!\n\nSeptember 26\, from 10 AM until 6 PM\n\n**Artists who wou
 ld like to participate with a booth and art** **for sale\, please see the
  guidelines.**
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/2026-healdsburg-arts-festival/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://redwoodwriters.org/robin-gabbert-the-magic-of-ekphrastic/", "Press Democrat": "https://redwoodwriters.org/robin-gabbert-the-magic-of-ekphrastic/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://redwoodwriters.org/robin-gabbert-the-magic-of-ekphrastic/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers Meeting--Robin Gabbert: The Magic of Ekphrastic
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T133000
UID:260405-Rs0ZqFDGUKSCrk6J8PRUw
DESCRIPTION:Please bring something savory or sweet to share in our potluck
 !\n\nThe Magic of Ekphrastic\, where you’ll learn how to use artwork to 
 inspire your creative writing\, both poetry and prose. The aim is to enhan
 ce observational skill and generate creative responses in a fun\, interact
 ive environment. This session is suited for any writer interested in empow
 ering creativity\, finding ways to battle writer’s block\, exploring new
  perspectives\, and fostering a deeper appreciation of the visual arts. We
  hope you can join us in this space where where words and art meet.\n\nAbo
 ut the Presenter: Robin Gabbert is the winner of Redwood Writers’ 2025 F
 ran Claggett-Holland Award and is a Pushcart Poetry Prize nominee for her 
 poem The Palm Reader. In 2024\, her poem Invisible was a finalist in the S
 an Francisco Writers’ Conference Poetry Contest and she was long-listed 
 for the Frontier Poetry Tanka Challenge. Her book of ekphrastic poetry— 
 The Clandestine Life of Paintings\, in Poems was published in 2022 and a f
 ull-length book of poetry Somehow\, I Haven’t Drowned was published by B
 lue Light Press in August 2025. She has poetry in state\, national\, and i
 nternational poetry anthologies including the Ekphrastic Review.
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/robin-gabbert-the-magic-of-ekphrastic/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-the-artists/", "Press Democrat": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-the-artists/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-the-artists/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Emergence - Spring Through the Eyes of the Artists
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T160000
UID:260401o8YwEBtvzkOkm2kUDPWqXw
DESCRIPTION:"Emergence" brings together the Artists of Fulton Crossing to 
 explore what Spring means to their creative lives. Spring is more than a s
 eason. It's a metaphor. It's renewal\, risk\, color\, thawing\, blooming\,
  awakening\, and sometimes even struggles. The public is invited to enjoy 
 this free Art exhibit and to take time to wander through the artists studi
 os and gallery spaces. Meet the artists at our opening reception March 21s
 t. Upcoming Art Workshops: March 21: Painting Easter Cookies. April 18: Ci
 gar Box Collage. May 16: Succulent Garden Centerpiece. Make treasures to b
 ring home. All ages welcome. Materials provided. E-mail Brenda at nanaspre
 ttypaper@outlook.com for preregistration and workshop info.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-
 the-artists/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
