DESCRIPTION:“….Get ready for the super-entertaining sounds of local ba
 nd The Social Contractors. They totally rock\, in all the right ways…”
  - Argus-Courier\n\nJoin us after the Butter & Egg Days parade at the "Far
 mhouse Artisan Market Music Stage" \\(foot of B Street at the Petaluma Riv
 er Turning Basin\\) for an afternoon of upbeat original rock and classic h
 its from the 60s-90s \\(Beatles\, Hendrix\, Pink Floyd\, Tom Petty\, Polic
 e\, Doors\, Steely Dan\, U2\, Men at Work\, and more\\)! \n\nThe Social C
 ontractors will be performing with a special lineup including local "all s
 tars" Travis Thayer \\(Cozy Cats\, Blue 7\\) on sax/keys/vocals\, Rob Neid
 el \\(Hyperdrive Kittens\\) on bass\, Chris Oatman \\(The Receders\\) on d
 rums\, and special guest\, Robert Ramirez \\(Cozy Cats\, Mighty Groove\\) 
 on percussion.\n\nWhether you like melodic vocals\, searing solos\, intrig
 uing lyrics\, or just great dynamic and danceable rhythms\, The Social Con
 tractors won't disappoint. \n\nhttps://petalumadowntown.com/butter-eggs-p
 arade.html
