BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/thoreau-back-to-nature-a-free-film-screening-discussion-tickets-1985597939889"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Thoreau: Back to Nature\, a Free Film Screening & Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260418T163000
UID:260408DL-H_69Rj02RNHgJ2KaONA
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the beautiful Heron Hall for a free screening event
 —co-sponsored by the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation and Northern Califo
 rnia Public Media\, and generously supported by Sonoma Water—followed by
  a community discussion and nature walk inspired by the new documentary *H
 enry David Thoreau*\, produced by Ken Burns and featuring Jeff Goldblum an
 d George Clooney.\n\nThis special gathering explores themes of environment
 al stewardship\, expanding access to nature\, and the timeless quest for a
 n authentic life—core ideas rooted in Thoreau’s philosophy.\n\nFollowi
 ng the screening\, enjoy a moderated panel discussion featuring Jack Hines
 \, Soundscape Ecologist and host of *Ear to the Wild*\, and Meilin Tsao\, 
 a local agriculturalist. Together\, they’ll reflect on how these ideas c
 ome to life through their work and experiences here in Sonoma County.\n\nW
 e’ll conclude the afternoon with a guided nature walk through the native
  plant garden—an opportunity to connect more deeply with the landscape t
 hat inspires this conversation.\n\nThis event offers a unique blend of fil
 m\, discussion\, and outdoor experience\, inviting our community to engage
 \, reflect\, and reconnect with the natural world. We hope to see you ther
 e! This event is free\, but space is limited—RSVP today!
LOCATION:Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/thoreau-back-to-nature-a-free-film-screen
 ing-discussion-tickets-1985597939889
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
