DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T153000
UID:260324cX8KOJGA-0-1QO0OtlOoig
DESCRIPTION:Cinnabar Theater presents The Christians by Lucas Hnath\n\nA p
 owerful\, thought-provoking drama about faith\, conviction\, and the cost 
 of standing by your beliefs.\n\nWhen a beloved megachurch pastor delivers 
 a sermon that challenges a core doctrine\, his congregation is thrown into
  turmoil. What follows is an intimate and gripping exploration of belief\,
  doubt\, leadership\, and community—inviting audiences to wrestle with b
 ig questions that linger long after the final moment on stage.\n\n• Warr
 en Theater\, Sonoma State University \\(Ives Hall\\)\, 1801 East Cotati Av
 e\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\n• April 10–26\, 2026\n\n• Fridays & S
 aturdays at 7:30 PM | Sundays at 2:00 PM\n\n• Special Talkback Post Show
 : Sunday\, April 19\n\nDirected by Nathan Cummings and featuring a stellar
  cast\, this minimalist\, emotionally resonant production is recommended f
 or mature audiences.\n\nTickets: cinnabartheater.org
LOCATION:Sonoma State University
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thechristians/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026-apjourn", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/slow-wildflower-journey/18329580/2026-04-19T14"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026-apjourn"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Slow Wildflower Journey
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T160000
UID:260315rsFlhnZmFE6cdoNPhsPQ4Q
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbirds\, the taste of a Douglas Fir
  needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or w
 atching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and ins
 ects in the grass? Join Certified California Naturalists and Suga
 rloaf docents for this series of meandering Sunday afternoon expl
 orations. Each month (weather permitting) we will explore one or
  two of our accessible trails-- the Creekside Nature Trail\, and
  the Meadow Trail. Suitable for all levels and a range of mobi
 lity\, these Sunday afternoon adventures will accommodate people u
 sing walkers or wheelchairs\, young children\, parents with babies
  in strollers\, as well as those who just enjoy slow walks in
  nature that stimulate the five senses. Our April outing will f
 ocus on the wildflowers of Sugarloaf.\n\nTickets are $5 for adult
 s and free for children under 18 years of age (a parent or le
 gal guardian must accompany minors). Meet at the White Barn park
 ing lot. There will be frequent stops and opportunities for conv
 ersation\, photography\, nature journaling\, wildlife viewing\, rest
 ing\, etc.\, so bring your nature journal\, camera\, or binocular
 s if you have them. Wear comfortable shoes\, a hat\, sun protec
 tion\, bring water and if desired\, a snack. Parking fees apply.
  Rain cancel. In the event of rain\, we will reschedule to Sun
 day\, April 12\, at the same time.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026-apjourn
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107917926?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Lauren Jenkins
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T000000
UID:260312Uap6Q0vIUUuf3iOf-iypOQ
DESCRIPTION:Americana singer-songwriter Lauren Jenkins has been a touring 
 artist since she was 15 years old. The Texas born\, Carolina-raised artist
  chose a life that would fit perfectly in the songs she writes: across cou
 ntless smoky bars\, fake IDs\, and endless miles on the road\, music has b
 een her one constant companion. Named an Artist to Watch by the New York T
 imes\, Billboard\, Rolling Stone\, Pandora\, and many more\, she was also 
 chosen as a member of the “Class of 2019” by influential radio DJ Bobb
 y Bones\, and made her TODAY Show debut as Elvis Duran’s Artist of the M
 onth. An accomplished actress and filmmaker\, Lauren wrote\, produced\, an
 d starred in an original short film titled 'Running Out of Road' that acco
 mpanied the release of her critically-acclaimed debut album\, NO SAINT\,  
 on Big Machine Records. Her short film"Running Out Of Road" was an officia
 l selection at Roswell Film Festival and screened during the Nashville Fil
 m Festival\, SXSW\, and Sundance. \n\nShe has hosted as a Guest DJ on Siri
 us XM's E Street channel. Her love of Bruce Springsteen compelled her to r
 ecord two of the Bosses songs "Stolen Car" and "Hungry Heart"\, which also
  debuted on the E Street Channel. \n\nLauren has built a loyal following i
 n Europe and the UK after her debut at C2C festival in March of 2019. Just
  before the world shut down in 2020 Lauren was just coming home from a suc
 cessiful tour in Europe and the UK. \n\nSince the pandemic\, Lauren has be
 en connecting with audiences through virtual "living room concerts" until 
 she can get back on the road. \n\nIn May of 2020\, she released “Ain’t
  That Hard\,” her first song as a fully independent artist. Part 1 of he
 r sophomore record "Miles On Me" is out now.\n\n"“Lauren is unapologetic
 ally raw at times\, uncompromising and unflinching in the way she looks at
  the world and herself. If you are looking for someone with meaning\, some
 one with a knack for melody and someone with an honest\, authentic view of
  life\, love and relationships\, then Lauren Jenkins always has been\, and
  even more now\, is the perfect artist for you.” - Lyric Magazine
LOCATION:Brasswood Cellars
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107917926?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/head-over-heels/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Head Over Heels
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T161500
UID:250801ZV0E3R5vY0669gs2ybuaJA
DESCRIPTION:**A Kingdom at Risk\, a Beat That Won’t Quit\, and Love That
  Rules All!**\n\n***“It’s a feel good riot from start to finish.“* 
 — Jay Darcy\, Mancunion Media Group** \n\n**Get ready for a wild\, laugh
 -out-loud adventure with *HEAD OVER HEELS*—the electrifying musical come
 dy from the creative forces behind Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, Avenue Q\, 
 and Spring Awakening! Nominated for *Outstanding New Broadway Musical* in 
 2019 and powered by the chart-topping hits of the legendary all-female roc
 k band The Go-Go’s\, this high-energy show features beloved anthems like
  “We Got the Beat\,” “Our Lips Are Sealed\,” “Vacation\,” “H
 eaven is a Place on Earth\,” and “Mad About You.”**\n\n**Join a spir
 ited royal family on a whirlwind quest to save their kingdom from doom—o
 nly to realize that the key to their future isn’t written in fate\, but 
 in their own hearts. Packed with irresistible music\, over-the-top comedy\
 , and a whole lot of love\, *HEAD OVER HEELS* is a dazzling\, feel-good sp
 ectacle that will have you dancing in your seat!**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays 
 & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: Two hours
 \, 15 mins including intermission\n\nThursdays Adult $33Fri/Sat Eve Adult 
 $44.95\; Senior $38.95\; Under 18 $31.95Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $55.95\; Sen
 ior $48.95Value seating $37.95\\*All prices include fees(707) 523-4185**bo
 xoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/head-over-heels/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
