X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/events/trashion-fashion/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Cory Infinite Artist Talk & Book Signing
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260420T173000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260420T193000
UID:260411L4delKx0bU-WMw7f4dnpfA
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, April 20 from 5:30PM – 7:30 PM\n\nLocated in the Se
 cret Garden at the Sonoma Community Center Free to attend\, RSVP - please 
 see website\n\nPaper-Back and Hard-Cover copies of his book will be availa
 ble for purchase and signing\n\nCory Infinite is a self taught fashion des
 igner from Kansas City\, Missouri that creates clothes from recycled mater
 ials and sometimes trash. Ever since graduating high school in 2020 Cory h
 as built a following of over 830K across Instagram and Tiktok and has work
 ed with brands and musicians such as: Converse\, Ripley’s Believe it or 
 not\, Erykah Badu\, A$AP Rocky\, UFO361\, Yung Lean\, Teezo Touchdown\, Ma
 gdalena Bay\, 347 Aidan and more. Cory’s pieces have appeared in Vogue G
 ermany and have been worn on stage at Coachella\, Dave Chappelle’s Night
  Club\, and on Jimmy Kimmel Live TV. Cory has appeared in Newsweek and on 
 Fox 4 KC two times now. The Cory Infinite brand stands for sustainability\
 , positivity\, creativity\, inclusivity and infinite human potential. Cory
  Infinite seeks to encourage others to tap into their infinite potential a
 nd use what’s already around them to the best of their ability. Cory wil
 l also be a guest judge for our Trashion Fashion Runway Show.\n\nPaper-Bac
 k and Hard-Cover copies of his book will be available for purchase and sig
 ning at the artist talk. Check out the book - please see website
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/events/trashion-fashion/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/paint-out-gear-up-preparing-to-paint-en-plein-air/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Paint Out Gear Up: Preparing to Paint en Plein Air
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260420T173000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260420T193000
UID:260410vR1Zy-6LDEyaGMiZ0NIRdA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nMonday\, April 20\, 2026 5:30 PM – 7:30 PM\n\nLo
 cation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: 
 Drawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nAge(s)\n\n18 and older\n\nTotal Registra
 tion Cost:\n\n**Free**\n\nLearn plein air painting with Michael Bartlett. 
 Master outdoor gear for oil\, watercolor\, and pastel in this expert-led w
 orkshop. Sign up today!\n\nAbout the Class\n\nPainting outdoors on locatio
 n is a wonderful way to connect with nature and keep you in the moment. If
  you’d like to start plein air painting\, here is your chance to learn w
 hat equipment and supplies are needed. What is a pochade box and do you ne
 ed one? Michael Bartlett will share his considerable knowledge to help you
  get started – and spare you from lugging too much up a mountain or out 
 to the beach. Bring a notebook to write down valuable tips. Though this wo
 rkshop is oriented for oil painters it also applies to other outdoor mediu
 ms such as watercolor\, gouache\, and pastel. This workshop is the perfect
  lead-in to Michael’s class **Plein Air Oil Painting: Chromatics in the 
 Wild** which starts on May 4th.
