SUMMARY:Ellie James & Loralee Christensen
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T180000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T000000
UID:260224_Bk3TkNPd0Ga3pan8EDynw
DESCRIPTION:Your new favorite song is just around the corner. Enter the wo
 rld of singer-songwriter and producer Ellie James\, and treat yourself to 
 a show unlike any you've ever seen. Stylistically unique and captivating\,
  Ellie James mixes lush indie-pop sounds with the style and edge of her ro
 ck ’n’ roll background. Her music is both genuine and dance-inducing\,
  as she uses real instruments and electronic production to weave musical s
 tories all her own. Ellie has been performing professionally all over the 
 world for more than 10 years\, most recently opening up for Grammy-winning
  artist Colbie Caillat\, and playing to electric audiences at Hollywood’
 s famous Viper Room and San Francisco’s Cafe du Nord. With the release o
 f her much-anticipated sophomore EP “Favorite Stranger” and a nearly s
 old-out headlining show at Hopmonk\, Ellie shows no signs of stopping with
  a year ahead full of new shows\, new merch\, and new music.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107729863?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-poetry-month", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/poetry-month-writing-printing-workshop-series/18131346/2026-04-22T18"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-poetry-month"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Poetry Month Writing & Printing Workshop Series
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T180000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260422T203000
UID:260216-EHrEl3D1USL7HQVLbk3zw
DESCRIPTION:Each week\, we’ll warm up with guided poetry prompts and gro
 up workshopping\, then move into spontaneous composition using movable met
 al and wood type. You’ll set short poems by hand\, experiment with layou
 t and typography\, and print your work on the press—embracing the beauti
 ful constraints and surprises of letterpress.\n\nAs the weeks progress\, w
 e’ll curate and print a collaborative chapbook featuring original poems 
 from everyone in the group. The final result will be a shared\, tactile pu
 blication that reflects a month of creative exchange\, ink-stained hands\,
  and collective storytelling.\n\nNo prior letterpress or poetry experience
  is required—just curiosity\, openness\, and a willingness to play with 
 language and form. Whether you’re a seasoned poet or brand new to writin
 g\, this workshop offers space to experiment\, connect\, and make somethin
 g meaningful together.\n\n*All materials included. Participants will recei
 ve copies of the finished chapbook.*
LOCATION:North Bay Letterpress Arts
URL:https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-poetry-month
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
