SUMMARY:The 9th Annual We the Future Social Justice Conference!
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T090000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T143000
UID:260308mf-q9QgOr0qR3WM_rw3Fhw
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, April 24\, 2026\,  from 9:00am – 2:30pm\, Santa Ro
 sa Junior College and North Bay Organizing Projects invites you to attend 
 the 9th Annual We the Future Social Justice Conference! \n\nThis year’s
  conference centers the truth that joy and resistance are not opposites 
 — they are intertwined liberatory practices. Joy fuels resistance. Resis
 tance protects the conditions for joy. Together\, they form the heartbeat 
 of collective liberation.\n\nWe the Future 2026 calls us to gather\, learn
 \, heal\, create\, and act together — rooting in joy\, practicing resist
 ance\, and shaping liberatory futures in community. We are thrilled to wel
 come this year’s keynote speaker\, Prisca Dorcas Mojica Rodríguez\, who
  is a writer\, organizer\, and public intellectual whose work centers the 
 lived experiences of undocumented and formerly undocumented Latine communi
 ties.\n\nCome and explore through three pathways: Educate. Activate. Creat
 e. \n\nSave your spot and register to attend this free event at **wethefu
 ture.santarosa.edu.**
LOCATION:Petaluma SRJC
URL:https://wethefuture.santarosa.edu/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
