BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/trashion-print-lab-tetra-pak-milk-carton-printing/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:“Trashion” Print Lab: Tetra Pak & Milk Carton Printing
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T173000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T193000
UID:260410cuUYqW8zKEaRCdc859PHmA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nFriday\, April 24\, 2026 5:30 PM – 7:30 PM\n\nLo
 cation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: 
 Printmaking\, Sustainability\n\nAge(s)\n\n16+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$15
 \n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n**$15**\n\nI
 n honor of “Trashion Fashion” we are focusing on creative reuse\, and 
 sustainable printmaking! \n\nAbout the Class\n\nRoll up your sleeves and 
 join us for a special evening of “Trashion” Print Lab! Our mission is 
 to explore a creative arts technique socially with our community. Print La
 b is not a traditional class\, but an affordable art-making experience. We
  welcome you to print\, play and experiment with an activity to create som
 ething unique in our printmaking studio!  **In honor of “Trashion Fashi
 on” we are focusing on creative reuse\, and sustainable printmaking! **
  Tetra Pak printmaking is an eco-friendly and accessible art technique tha
 t repurposes used food and beverage cartons – like those for milk\, juic
 e\, or broth\, as printing plates. It is a form of intaglio printmaking (s
 imilar to drypoint etching)\, where you scratch or “incise” a design i
 nto the carton’s inner foil or plastic lining to create a printable surf
 ace. Carton printing is widely considered a highly sustainable alternative
  to traditional etching because it prioritizes creative reuse and non-toxi
 c processes. Recycle\, repurpose and recreate! Learn how to turn garbage i
 nto beautiful prints! We will demonstrate how to draw\, scratch\, cut\, in
 k and print carton surfaces on our presses with water-soluble etching inks
 . Guests will leave with their own prints they create! ***We have plenty o
 f cartons to share\, but we encourage guests to bring their own cleaned Te
 tra Pak’s and milk cartons to use or donate to the printmaking studio.**
 * No printmaking experience is necessary. Light refreshments will be provi
 ded.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/trashion-print-lab-tetra-pa
 k-milk-carton-printing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
