X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Throwing Skills Workshop with Visiting Artist Amy Palatnick
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T160000
UID:260324mE9LzdeyZEWAvDHjXi6fgQ
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, April 25\, 2026 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\
 nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediat
 e and Advanced\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n
 17\\+\n\n$165 – Registration Cost \\(Includes Clay\\)\n\nLearn essential
  body care practices and master the Claw Pull technique in this immersive 
 one-day pottery workshop with full-time Studio Potter Amy Palatnick.\n\nAb
 out the Class\n\nJoin full time Studio Potter Amy Palatnick for an immersi
 ve one-day workshop designed to support your body in the studio and streng
 then your foundational wheelthrowing technique. Body and Self-Care in the 
 Studio: Start the day by learning essential practices for sustaining a lon
 g\, healthy\, and joyful pottery life. Amy will guide you through practica
 l body-care strategies that promote alignment\, ease\, and comfort as you 
 work—helping you prevent strain\, reduce soreness\, and feel more comfor
 table as you work. The Claw Pull Technique\; In the afternoon\, you’ll d
 ive into Amy’s signature Claw Pull—the foundational technique first pu
 ll that moves a lot of clay and sets you up for strong\, even-walled cylin
 ders. Through demonstration\, guided practice\, and personalized feedback\
 , you’ll begin building the muscle memory and confidence to integrate th
 is transformative technique into your throwing.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/throwing-skills-workshop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/calming-the-restless-mind-hc2d26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/calming-the-restless-mind/18363181/2026-04-25T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/calming-the-restless-mind-hc2d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Calming the Restless Mind
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T150000
UID:260324eBhVIWU-30yMbPNAxTMk9g
DESCRIPTION:with Howard Cohn\n\nEveryone wants to be calm and peaceful. Re
 stlessness and agitation can arise when the mind is unsettled\, the heart 
 is reactive\, and our perception of the present moment is unclear. During 
 this day together\, we will explore ways of steadying the heart and mind s
 o that calm in the present moment becomes more accessible\, insight devel
 ops naturally\, and the heart softens.\n\nDuring this daylong\, we will dr
 aw on the Four Foundations of Mindfulness—being mindful of and sensitive
  to our bodies—beginning with the sensations of breathing\, and expandin
 g to include other physical sensations. We will explore how to feel pleasu
 re more fully without trying to make it last\, and how to more easily acco
 mmodate unpleasant experiences without becoming overwhelmed or reactive. W
 e will also practice recognizing and working with our emotions\, while lea
 rning how to relate to our thoughts more kindly and skillfully rather than
  being so easily carried away by them.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/calming-the-restless-m
 ind-hc2d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
