BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108014161?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T123000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T000000
UID:260327MQAzR-3PWEKOpnFMDcBm1Q
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108014161?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.earthlyprocession.com/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.earthlyprocession.com/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.earthlyprocession.com/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Earthly Procession
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T123000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T160000
UID:260325N8Cof-lo_kezhblz8eMbSw
DESCRIPTION:This April\, the streets will see something new – a parade o
 f larger-than-life moths\, migratory birds\, and other regional species. S
 anta Rosa artist-biologist Alina Nuebel\, the Santa Rosa Urban Arts Partne
 rship\, and community community partners\, with support from the City of S
 anta Rosa\, will be hosting the Earthly Procession – a parade to celebra
 te regional pride in our local natural environment\, raise awareness of th
 e environmental issues that are close to home\, and the tangible solutions
  that every person can implement for immediate results. Taking place in Sa
 nta Rosa’s underutilized bike and pedestrian infrastructure\, the Proces
 sion will be a joyous occupation of non-car spaces around downtown. Everyo
 ne is welcome to join\, and strongly encouraged to make or bring art of lo
 cal species. The Procession will meet at Juilliard Park at 12:00\, and wil
 l depart for Court House Square at 12:30. Once the parade arrives\, it wil
 l integrate with the Santa Rosa Earth Day Festival to display art and offe
 r interactive\, educational art activities.
LOCATION:Courthouse Square
URL:https://www.earthlyprocession.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
