BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/self-defense/18338080/2026-04-25T13"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Self-Defense
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T130000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T150000
UID:260319DcvlrsEAmk2SLr1BLyoRLQ
DESCRIPTION:Are you prepared to face the unexpected? Join us for self-def
 ense class\n\nIn a world that demands alertness\, knowing how to protect y
 ourself is not a luxury—it’s a necessity. Join our intensive 2 HOURS 
 Self-Defense class lesson \\(\\+ stay extra hour if you want to just pract
 ice\\) class designed to give you the fundamental tools\, techniques\, and
  mindset needed for immediate safety.\n\nThis highly condensed course focu
 ses on awareness\, prevention\, and simple\, effective physical responses
  you can rely on when seconds count. We prioritize getting you to safety 
 above all else.\n\nWorkshop Details\n\nThe “Airway Priority”: techniq
 ue to instantly break front and rear chokes\, ensuring you can breathe and
  think clearly under pressure.\n\nClothing & Control: Discover how to use
  an attacker’s grip against them. We’ll cover shirt and lapel grabs\, 
 teaching you how to use leverage to break their “frame” and create dis
 tance.\n\nAsset Defense \\(Backpacks & Purses\\): Most thefts involve a g
 rab of your gear. We’ll practice how to defend against being dragged by 
 a strap\, when to “shed the load\,” and how to use your bag as a tempo
 rary shield.\n\nCounter-Striking Foundations: Learn to use “biological 
 tools”—palm strikes\, knees\, and elbows—to disrupt an attacker’s 
 focus so you can facilitate your release.\n\nImportant Details\n\nPlease w
 ear non-marking shoe soles: This helps us keep our floors in great condi
 tion.\n\n2 HOURS Self-Defense class lesson \\(\\+ stay extra hour if you w
 ant to just practice\\)\n\nDate: April 25\, 2026\n\nTIME: 1:00 PM – 3:00
  PM \\(\\+ extra practice if you want to stay until 4:00 PM\\)\n\nAddress:
  4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes befo
 re.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/self-defense/18338080/2
 026-04-25T13
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/por-la-luz-de-la-luna-a-mexican-ballet/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.sonomadance.org/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/por-la-luz-de-la-luna-a-mexican-ballet/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Por la Luz de la Luna: A Mexican Ballet
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T130000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T150000
UID:260401n_VthTFMaUuQXwRYjtPuQQ
DESCRIPTION:This original ballet libretto was inspired by award-winning au
 thor and arts activist Aida Salazar's story of her great-aunt\, Jovita Val
 dovinos\, who fought for religious freedom in Mexico's Cristero War in the
  1930s.Por la Luz de la Lunabrings a fictional account of Jovita's story t
 o life\, weaving history\, mythology\, and family legacy into a powerful t
 heatrical experience while celebrating her heroism. As one of the few Mexi
 can-themed ballets in history\, it creates a space for dancers of all back
 grounds to portray Latina/o characters\, highlighting unique stories and h
 onoring Mexican and Mexican-American heritage on stage. Set to 20th-centur
 y Mexican classical music by composers such as Carlos Chávez and José Pa
 blo Moncayo\, the ballet is brought to life through striking sets and Azte
 c-inspired costumes designed by visual artist PEMEX. It premiered on April
  9\, 2016\, at the Sebastiani Theatre and continues to be a highlight of t
 he company's repertory.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/por-la-luz-de-la-luna-a-mexican-balle
 t/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
