BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.inspirenapavalley.org/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.inspirenapavalley.org/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.inspirenapavalley.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Inspire Napa Valley Event Support Alzheimer’s and Dementia Resea
 rch
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260426T100000
UID:2603095jIA_ACLckWQltOAUig26Q
DESCRIPTION:The seventh annual Inspire Napa Valley will take place from Fr
 iday\, April 24 – Sunday\, April 26 in Napa Valley. Hosted by Kerrin L
 az\, founder of K. LAZ WINE COLLECTION\, the wine community and beyond to
  raise funds and awareness to advance Alzheimer’s and dementia research
  nationally and enhance local care and support services for impacted fami
 lies. Since its inception in 2017\, the event has raised over $9 milli
 on for these vital efforts. This impactful event continues to unite win
 e industry leaders and enthusiasts to raise awareness\, spark change\, a
 nd secure national funding for an incredible cause. Don't miss out on 
 this inspiring weekend that combines the best of Napa Valley with a commi
 tment to making a difference!Events include:\n\nFriday\, April 24 | VIP We
 lcome Dinner – The Best of Oakville\n\n5:30 PM | Gamble Estates\, Oakvil
 le\, CA\n\nAn exclusive evening\, The Best of Oakville\, brings together e
 ight of the region’s best wineries as co-hosts\, sharing their stories a
 nd wines\, from rare library selections to current releases. The experienc
 e is paired with a wine country feast led by Napa Valley’s own Chef Sean
  Massey and joined in the kitchen by some of wine country’s leading vint
 ners\, winemakers\, growers\, and industry icons. This intimate gathering 
 captures the spirit of true wine country hospitality.\n\nThe wineries incl
 ude Dalla Valle Vineyards\, Gamble Estates\, Harlan Estate\, Opus On\, Scr
 eaming Eagle\, Tench Vineyards\, VHR – Vine Hill Ranch\, FUTO\n\nSaturda
 y\, April 25 | VIP Alzheimer’s Research Update & Wine Tasting Seminar: D
 eep Dive Into Oakville’s Best\n\n10 AM | The Culinary Institute of Ameri
 ca at Greystone\, St. Helena\, CA\n\nFollowing an Alzheimer’s and dement
 ia research update from Inspire Napa Valley’s Scientific Advisors\, incl
 uding Gates Ventures’ Senior Director of Health & Life Sciences\, Farhad
  Imam\, guests will enjoy an in-depth exploration of six of Oakville’s m
 ost exceptional wines\, led by a distinguished panel including Antonio Gal
 loni\, founder of Vinous\, and Ray Isle\, Executive Wine Editor of Food & 
 Wine.\n\nIncluded for VIP guests. A limited number of seats are available 
 for main event guests.\n\nSaturday\, April 25 | Grand Wine Tasting\, Recep
 tion\, Dinner & Auction\n\n5 PM | Louis Martini Winery\, St. Helena\, CA\n
 \nEnjoy the walk-around Grand Tasting featuring more than 35 of California
 ’s most iconic wineries\, alongside a selection of exciting rising star 
 producers\, followed by a festive wine country dinner and Inspire Napa Val
 ley’s signature live auction and paddle raise.\n\nSunday\, April 26 | VI
 P Farewell Brunch\n\n10 AM | Ad Hoc + Addendum Garden\n\nA farewell brunch
  featuring Chef Thomas Keller’s Ad Hoc fried chicken and waffles\, along
 side Bouchon seasonal dishes and a classic bloody mary and mimosa bar.
LOCATION:Louis Martini Winery
URL:https://www.inspirenapavalley.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-wood-engraving", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/wood-engraving-2-day-intensive-workshop/18131355/2026-04-26T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-wood-engraving"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Wood Engraving - 2 Day Intensive Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260426T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260426T150000
UID:260216If5po8g_J0GAHe3XHFCSjQ
DESCRIPTION:This two-day workshop introduces the art and practice of wood 
 engraving. The hard woods used to make wood engraving blocks are type-high
  (.918”\, the height of metal type) and are cut across the grain rather 
 than parallel to it like wood cuts. These durable end-grain blocks allow f
 or extensive detail. The tools used are gravers (or burins) that are diffe
 rent than the gouge tools used for wood cuts. This versatile form of print
 making requires little space and minimal equipment and is perfect for a sm
 all home studio.\n\nDay 1: We will start with a brief history of wood engr
 aving including its long relationship to letterpress printing\, and we wil
 l study examples of period and contemporary wood engravings. Students will
  begin with a sampler block to explore the effects of various tools\, pro
 of the block on the press\, and transfer a design onto another block to c
 onsider the approach for their first engraving.\n\nDay 2: Students will l
 earn how to sharpen their gravers and continue to engrave their blocks. We
  will become familiar with basic use of the Vandercook SP-15 cylinder pres
 s to ink and proof the block and troubleshoot issues when printing. Printi
 ng an edition of a block will be discussed\, and those wanting to contribu
 te a print to the workshop portfolio are encouraged to do so. Students wil
 l leave the workshop with the skills to master the graver tool to create i
 ntricate prints\, a value test block for future reference\, an instructive
  handout\, a block to edition\, and a portfolio of workshop prints.\n\nLev
 el: Beginner – no previous experience necessary\n\n*Includes $50 materia
 ls fee\, which covers #3 elliptical tint tool and two 3”x 4” end-grain
  maple blocks)*\n\n**INSTRUCTOR**\n\n**Colleen Dwire** initially learned w
 ood engraving in a workshop with American Master John DePol and has been p
 racticing for over thirty years. She exhibits her prints internationally. 
 Colleen is an elected member of the Society of Wood Engravers (UK) and ser
 ves as Secretary and Exhibitions Officer for Wood Engravers’ Network (US
 A) and as a board member of North Bay Letterpress Arts. Learn more at www.
 colleendwire.com and follow on colleendwire.bsky.social.
LOCATION:North Bay Letterpress Arts
URL:https://www.northbayletterpressarts.org/for-sale/2026-wood-engraving
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
