SUMMARY:Exploring Botanical Monotypes
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260426T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260426T170000
UID:260410KYyM6vcjKUOx31rgQqBuow
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, April 26\, 2026 11:00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nE
 xperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nEvent Category: Printmaking\n\nAge(s)\n\n1
 8 and older\n\n**$140** – Registration Cost **$25** – Materials Fee **
 $165** – Total Registration Cost\n\nCreate stunning botanical monotype p
 rints with spring foliage in this inspiring workshop—perfect for beginne
 rs and plant lovers alike!\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nLearn to make stunning\,
  one-of-a-kind botanical prints inspired from the natural world! Join Kell
 y in this one-day experimental monotype printmaking workshop where you wil
 l explore techniques on the printing press. Students will learn how to ach
 ieve unique color compositions using local flora as stencils through simpl
 e layering and masking in a supportive group learning environment. Guests 
 are invited to print using a wide variety of spring foliage and preserved 
 botanicals. Kelly will also discuss and demonstrate how to add dimension t
 o prints by using textures\, mixed media and collage. It is sure to be a f
 un and awe-inspiring class for beginners or even experienced printmakers i
 nterested in learning a beautiful new technique. If you love plants\, and 
 you’ve always wanted to try monotype\, this class is sure to motivate an
 d inspire you!\n\nMembership has its benefits\n\nAll **Silver Memberships*
 * and above receive **10% off the registration cost for any class purchase
  over $40**. Materials fees are not discounted.\n\nBecome a member today a
 nd find community\, connection\, and creativity.\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/exploring-botanical-monotyp
 es/
