X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.duckhorn.com/events/event-calendar/discussion-and-derby-party", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/11th-annual-duckhorn-vineyards-derby-party-and-discussion-release/17913626/2026-05-02T13"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.duckhorn.com/events/event-calendar/discussion-and-derby-party"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:11th Annual Duckhorn Vineyards Derby Party and Discussion Release
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T133000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T163000
UID:260120rNdYuMp4Gk-CyMHqJhuROQ
DESCRIPTION:This year\, we’re bringing the festivities to a new setting 
 at our sister property\, The Duckhorn Collection at Paraduxx\, where the l
 egacy continues in a fresh new way.\n\nSettle into the day with Southern-i
 nspired bites from our new Culinary team led by Chef Dominic Orsini and ou
 r signature wines poured across our lounge\, beneath the old oak tree\, an
 d beside the vines. From Duckhorn Vineyards to Goldeneye and beyond\, expe
 rience the spirit of The Duckhorn Collection as our home becomes yours for
  an afternoon of food\, wine\, and celebration.\n\nTradition and excellenc
 e unite as we debut the 16th vintage of The Discussion Red Blend—a wine 
 that embodies the ongoing dialogue of craftsmanship and connection in wine
 making. Be among the first to savor the new 2022 vintage of this Bordeaux-
 inspired blend while reveling in the excitement of the 152nd Kentucky Derb
 y!\n\nNo Derby celebration would be complete without our Best Dressed Comp
 etition\, inviting guests to showcase their finest race-day style—from b
 ig hats and fascinators to sport coats and bow ties. For those seeking a t
 ouch more elegance and ease\, The Winner’s Circle offers relaxed comfort
  and curated service. Enjoy personalized wine selections and thoughtful pa
 irings\, with a dedicated host ensuring you won’t miss a moment of the a
 ction. From start to finish\, it’s an effortless\, unforgettable Duckhor
 n Derby Day.\n\n\\*Derby-inspired attire suggested.\n\n\\*\\*Guests must b
 e 21 and over to attend. No pets are allowed at this event.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Al
 l ticket sales are non-refundable
LOCATION:The Duckhorn Collection at Paraduxx
URL:https://www.duckhorn.com/events/event-calendar/discussion-and-derby-pa
 rty
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.guidedogs.com/about-guide-dogs-for-the-blind/graduations"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:GUIDE DOGS FOR THE BLIND'S GRADUATION CEREMONIES MELT HEARTS
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T133000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T143000
UID:260314bQ_nppKzBkS-t8hNDynXIA
DESCRIPTION:Guide Dogs for the Blind \\(GDB\\) will celebrate its guide d
 og team graduates every other Saturday with public graduation ceremonies a
 t the organization’s campus in San Rafael. These touching public events 
 have inspired tears in even the most stoic audience members\, as graduatin
 g guide dog teams proudly take the stage. Families are welcome at the cere
 monies\, which honor the independence and companionship that GDB’s gui
 de dogs provide for GDB’s clients who are blind or visually impaired. T
 he events also allow GDB’s clients to meet the puppy raisers who cared 
 for their canine heroes prior to beginning formal training at GDB’s cam
 pus. Ceremonies also recognize recent graduates of GDB’s Orientation an
 d Mobility \\(O&M\\) Program\, K9 Buddy Program\, and Breeder Dog Program
 .\n\nAdmission is free\, and Kleenex will be provided. Pre-registered bus 
 groups are welcome. Public tours of the campus are offered on the days of 
 the ceremonies. Visit www.guidedogs.com for more information. Graduat
 ion events are also livestreamed at https://www.youtube.com/@gdb\\_offici
 al/streams.
LOCATION:Guide Dogs for the Blind
URL:https://www.guidedogs.com/about-guide-dogs-for-the-blind/graduations
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://lesliescatchard.com", "Press Democrat": "http://lesliescatchard.com"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://lesliescatchard.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Through Tamsen's Eyes... The Story of the Donner Party
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T151500
UID:260406wOWuGTuCekGLl-Yi22E0vw
DESCRIPTION:In 1846\, Tamsen Donner was a teacher\, a botanist\, and a mot
 her with a dream of opening an academy in the West. She didn’t know that
  a "shortcut" would turn a journey of hope into a harrowing fight for surv
 ival. Step into the Sierra Nevada snows and hear the untold story of the D
 onner Party through the eyes of the woman who lived it. A haunting\, first
 -person journey through history\, heartbreak\, and the ultimate test of th
 e human spirit.
LOCATION:Clear Heart
URL:http://lesliescatchard.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
