BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.srsymphony.org/event/shakespeare-in-music/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.srsymphony.org/event/shakespeare-in-music/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.srsymphony.org/event/shakespeare-in-music/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Symphony - Shakespeare in Music
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T213000
UID:251217OygD9_-LXUecYFfzTcKVYw
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare in Music\n\nMay 2\, 3 & 4\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\nFrancesco Lecce-Chong\, conductor\n\nClaire Huangci\,
  piano\n\nNicola Vann\, actor\n\nSAMUEL COLERIDGE-TAYLOR: Incidental Music
  from Othello\n\nWOLFGANG AMADEUS MOZART: Concerto No. 20 in D minor for P
 iano and Orchestra\, K. 466\n\nPYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Hamlet \\(Fantasy
  Overture\\) in F minor\, Opus 67\n\nPYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Romeo and J
 uliet \\(Fantasy Overture\\) in B minor\n\nStep into the world of Shakespe
 are’s dramatic\, enduring tales. Tchaikovsky’s passionate Romeo and Ju
 liet is a timeless and familiar classic\, while Coleridge-Taylor’s evoca
 tive Othello offers a compelling counterpoint for interpreting Shakespeare
  in music. Plus\, pianist Claire Huangci makes her Weill Hall debut with M
 ozart’s expressive Piano Concerto No. 20.\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\
 , and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject to 
 availability.\n\nPhoto by  Jean-Baptiste Millot
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/shakespeare-in-music/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
