UID:260324VraB-E3kA0KuHePfYWc9QA
DESCRIPTION:No one taught the Buddha the Four Noble Truths. They arose fro
 m the insights of his own practice\, from looking deeply into the nature o
 f his experience. In this two-day program\, you’ll follow the same path 
 of discovery. Teachers Phillip Moffitt and Dana DePalma will guide you in 
 starting with the experience of your own life and building this understand
 ing from within. You’ll look directly at what causes your suffering and 
 explore the practical ways of relief available based on the Buddha’s tea
 chings. You’ll discover how the Four Noble Truths become the Four Ennobl
 ing Truths—not concepts to memorize\, but living insights that transform
  how you meet life\, by finding freedom and meaning in the midst of your c
 ircumstances.\n\nEach day will have periods of sitting and walking meditat
 ion along with Dharma talks\, discussion\, and Q&A.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/starting-with-our-exper
 ience-building-the-four-ennobling-truths/18363197/2026-05-03T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/53rd-annual-bodega-bay-fishermans-festival?aff=cityspark"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:53rd Annual Bodega Bay Fisherman's Festival
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260503T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260503T170000
UID:260316Uf9PYE0m2EewWTljPT-Lag
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 53rd Annual Bodega Bay Fisherman's Festival.\n
 \nDates: May 2nd &amp\; 3rd 2026\n\n10AM-5PM\n\nTheme: FISH TO DISH\n\nWel
 come to the Bodega Bay Fisherman's Festival\, a family friendly fundraiser
  for 25 local nonprofits. Since 1973\, this event has celebrated our local
  fisherman and it's when salmon season is kicked off with a blessing of th
 e fleet. The Festival is packed with events for people of all ages: over 6
 0 craft booths\, live music\, good food\, entertainment and more.\n\nThe F
 isherman's Festival is an all-volunteer event\, and proceeds benefit Bodeg
 a Bay Area community services.\n\n \n\nThe festival has its origin as a ce
 lebration of the start of the Salmon fishing season and the annual Blessin
 g of the Fleet. Each year's theme is chosen by the Bodega Bay Fisherman's 
 Marketing Association. At the Festival site itself\, you'll see a wooden b
 oat challenge where participating teams build a vessel and compete in a bo
 at race.  Sign up today https://www.bbfishfest.org/wooden-boat-challenge/\
 \#register\n\n \n\nA favorite attraction is the wine booth featuring more 
 than 25 Sonoma County wines and a beer booth with several local ales. Plus
  we have something for every palate\; barbecued oysters\, local fish &amp\
 ; chips\, clam chowder and a variety of non-seafood food trucks. Live musi
 c and entertainers perform on the main stage all day Saturday and Sunday. 
 Artisans and vendors from all over California and beyond offer a wide sele
 ction of arts and crafts.\n\n \n\nThe Fisherman's Festival is a great venu
 e for kids with a play area for face painting\, games\, a touch tank tide 
 pool\, jumpy houses\, pony rides. Leashed Pets are welcome and encouraged 
 to attend. Sunday morning will feature the Blessing of the Fishing Fleet w
 hen decorated boats parade out of the harbor to receive a blessing from lo
 cal clergy.\n\n \n\nLive Music All day on main stage\n\nSaturday May 2\n\n
 10am-11:30am The Rotten Tomatoes Rock Band\n\nNoon-2pm Dry Creek Station C
 ountry Band\n\n3pm-5pm Tainted Love- Best of the 80's Live\n\nSunday May 3
 \n\n10:30-Noon 40 Fathom's\n\n12:30 PM-2:15pm Petty Rocks - Tom Petty Cove
 r Band\n\n3PM-5PM Mustache Harbor\n\nVisit www.bbfishfest.org for more det
 ails\n\nParking Map \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n 
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/53rd-annual-bodega-bay-fis
 hermans-festival?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
