SUMMARY: Beginning Gel Printing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Magdalena Bogart\nMonday\, May 4th\n1:00pm-4:00PM
 \nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n$45.00\n\n\nJoin us for an inspiring gel pr
 inting workshop with Magdalena Bogart\, where you'll discover the\nmagic 
 of this versatile and expressive art form. You will learn techniques for 
 creating stunning\,\nlayered prints using gel plates\, rich textures\, an
 d vibrant colors.\nIf you have wanted to try out this fairly new and very
  popular way to make your own papers\, whether you are an experienced art
 ist or simply curious about the process\, this workshop will provide plen
 ty of creative inspiration and expert insights.\n\nDuring the 3-hours wor
 kshop\, you will learn the fundamentals of mono-printing with a gel plate
 \,\nincluding an in-depth look at the essential supplies needed. Magdalen
 a will discuss different\ntypes of plates and brayers\, as well as the wi
 de range of acrylic paints and inks. You will learn the basics of color t
 heory to ensure great results for your projects.\n\nYou will get to try o
 ut many fun techniques on different papers. Magdalena will introduce vari
 ous papers for gel printing\, including white copy paper\, calligraphy pa
 per\, deli paper\, marker paper\, and more each offering unique effects.\
 n\nThe workshop will also explore tools for making marks and textures\, f
 rom found objects to store-bought supplies. Magdalena will demonstrate ho
 w to use stencils - both handmade and purchased\, along with unconvention
 al tools like silicone scrapers\, scrapers\, bubble wrap\, buttons\, yarn
 \, and cardboard to create stunning patterns.\n\nShe will also cover tech
 niques to embellish your prints incorporating acrylic pens\, Inktense pen
 cils and other techniques.\nAdditionally\, Magdalena will provide expert 
 guidance on cleaning\, caring for\, and storing gel plates to ensure thei
 r longevity. To wrap up the session\, she will showcase creative ways to 
 use your printed papers\, including ideas for collages\, handmade cards\,
  and art journals\, along with a take-home list of even more ways to inco
 rporate your gel prints into future projects. Whether you are looking to 
 refine your skills or try something new\, this workshop promises to be an
  engaging and educational experience. Come explore the endless possibilit
 ies of gel printing.\n\n\nTo register for this workshop\, please contact 
 Magdalena at: 408.781.2589 or by email\nat: mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com m
 ailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bogart@
 gmail.com mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bog
 art@gmail.com
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,gel-printing
