BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/abstract-collage-minis-create-a-series-5/17"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Abstract Collage Minis - Create A Series — Sebastopol Center For
  the Arts\, California
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260517T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260518T000000
UID:c1a88ab7a62595336635fd6a8e8cc5b1@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Abstract Collage Minis - Create A Series\, 5/17\n\n  \n    \n 
      \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSunday\,
  May 17\, 2026\; 11 AM - 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials feeAge: 16+ In this
  new workshop\, French-American collage artist Catherine Cruz will teach y
 ou how to create a dynamic series of abstract collages using elements such
  as color\, line and shape.  You will work on four small wood panels to co
 mpose a cohesive series. Working on several panels at once offers several 
 advantages\, including greater creative momentum\, the ability to build a 
 strong thematic connection between pieces\, and a way to maintain creative
  flow.  This technique allows for a deeper exploration of an idea or theme
  than is possible with a single piece. We will start with short compositio
 n exercises to discuss design principles and abstraction.  Then Catherine 
 will demonstrate her method for mounting papers on the panels.  You will h
 ave ample time to select papers and create your designs. What you’ll lea
 rn from this workshop: Reliable method for layering collage papers\, Creat
 ive ways to explore abstraction\, Techniques for creating a cohesive serie
 s\, Strategies for refining your compositionIMPORTANT: Instructions for wh
 ere to purchase your materials and how to prepare them is provided in the 
 attached PDF. We will take a short break for lunch between 12:30 and 1:00 
 pm so please bring your lunch and a beverage.   About the instructor: Cath
 erine Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is informed by textures 
 and patterns created by the passing of time and the effects of the natural
  elements on the built environment.  She holds a Bachelor of Science in in
 terior design and she worked in the field of architectural design and gree
 n building certification for over 25 years.  She has taught collage and mi
 xed media workshops in the Bay Area and in France since 2019\, and this is
  her fifth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts.  Her studio is loca
 ted in Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails Open Studios.  You ma
 y contact Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Check out Catherine’s 
 other classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-classes. \n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n   
          \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/abstract-collage-minis-create
 -a-series-5/17
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/unlocking-the-power-of-your-iphone-camera"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Unlocking the Power of Your iPhone Camera — Sebastopol Center Fo
 r the Arts\, California
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260517T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260518T000000
UID:52d3a441691ee7c5806c6a9bb3c20062@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Unlocking the Power of Your iPhone Camera\n\n  \n    \n      \
 n        \n          $85.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSunday\, May 17
 \, 2026\; 12PM - 4PM$85.00A Creative Photography WorkshopThe powerful\, al
 ways-accessible iPhone camera makes it easier than ever to document your l
 ife-- you’re equipped to capture everything from everyday memories to st
 unning landscapes\, --all while enhancing your creativity.In this workshop
 \, we will explore the full potential of your iPhone camera. Through discu
 ssion and hands-on demonstrations\, we will cover:•  Camera settings and
  adjustments•  Filters\, exposure\, and focus•  Shutter speed and lens
  options (best use of all the lenses)•  Techniques for panoramas\, macro
  shots\, close-ups\, and portraits•  Compositional strategies to elevate
  your photographyThroughout\, we’ll emphasize the creative and artistic 
 aspects of photography—how to think about composition\, lighting\, and s
 torytelling to enhance your images.What to Bring: Your iPhone camera and
  a passion for creativity! This workshop is designed to inspire and equip 
 you with the skills to transform your photo-taking into an art form. Andro
 id phones are welcome\, but we will be demonstrating on an iPhone.  All iP
 hones and levels of photographic experience are welcome!!! You’ll learn 
 new techniques and settings that will elevate your photos\, enhance your m
 emories\, and open exciting new photographic possibilities.Join us to disc
 over how to “Find Your Vision” and unlock the full creative potential 
 of your iPhone camera!About the Instructors: As a husband-and-wife team\, 
 Susan and Neil Silverman have been “captured” with photography for ove
 r 25 years – teaching\, leading workshops and working professionally in 
 many venues. They have taught for the Kelby Photo Conferences\, Gualala Ar
 ts Center\, Santa Rosa Junior College\, Pacific Northwest Art School\, Poi
 nt Reyes Field Institute\, Great American Photography Workshop (GAPW)\, an
 d Better Photo\, as well as many photo clubs and organizations. Their work
  has been published both nationally and internationally. Sharing knowledge
 \, experiences and camaraderie is as important as “getting the shot.”\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n         
  \n            \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/unlocking-the-power-of-your-i
 phone-camera
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
